cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use snai-int8 or its measurement series, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "snai-int8: integer training of small transformer language models"
authors:
  - given-names: Sebastian
    family-names: Woratsch
    alias: komakeule57-maker
repository-code: "https://github.com/komakeule57-maker/snai-int8"
url: "https://github.com/komakeule57-maker/snai-int8"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.0.2"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
abstract: >-
  A research engine for int8 training of small transformer language models:
  int8 weights, integer matmuls in forward and backward with int32 gradient
  accumulation, and 8-bit Adam moments. Normalization, softmax, loss and the
  optimizer update are still computed in float. With SNAI_I8_REST=sr there
  is no per-weight floating-point state across steps. The engine is written
  in Nim with CPU (OpenMP), CUDA and OpenCL backends that are bit-identical
  to the CPU reference. The repository also contains the research log:
  measurement series, each with a pre-registered criterion, recipe, raw
  values and verdict.
keywords:
  - int8 training
  - quantized training
  - stochastic rounding
  - small language models
  - transformer
  - Nim
